[h1]Battlezone 98 Redux: Unofficial Community Patch, Visual Remaster & Campaign Rewrite[/h1]
[i]Three projects in one download: an open-source native engine patch that works game-wide, a remaster of the game's own models, textures, terrain, skies and UI, and a rewritten 17-mission campaign you can play solo or in four-player co-op.[/i]

[h2]Important Notice[/h2]
[b]This project is 100% unofficial and is not affiliated with or supported by Rebellion. It's functional and reasonably stable, but still under active development.[/b] It changes native game behavior, so expect bugs, crashes or differences from the unmodified game.

All source code is public on GitHub, so you can review it, contribute, or build it yourself. Game improvements should be open and verifiable, not hidden.

[h2]Install and Play[/h2]
[list=1]
[*] Subscribe and let Steam finish downloading. Do [b]not[/b] enable anything in the Mods menu.
[*] Launch the game and open [b]Single Player > Instant Action[/b] (bottom right).
[*] Start [b]! SETUP / REPAIR - Open Community Patch[/b]. It installs the complete OpenShim suite and shows the result.
[*] [b]Exit the game completely[/b], then start it again. The files are put in place while the game is closed.
[/list]

[b]The campaign:[/b] open [b]Single Player > Custom Campaign[/b] (top right) and choose [b]Campaign Reimagined[/b]: 17 NSDF missions from [b]Red Arrival[/b] to [b]The Ultimate Quake[/b] (the last few are still in development). Each is also a co-op map ([b]CR 01[/b] to [b]CR 17 Coop[/b]) for up to four players. All other content keeps its usual menus.

[b]Updating:[/b] automatic. When the Workshop item updates, the game stages the new OpenShim and installs it when you quit. You can also press [b]Check for Updates[/b] on [b]Options > OpenShim[/b] (Steam only). Run Setup / Repair again only if the install is damaged or the button is unavailable.

OpenShim validates the game build and patch sites, fails closed on a mismatch, and never modifies battlezone98redux.exe on disk. If setup fails, check [i]openshim_update.status[/i] and [i]winmm_replace.log[/i]. Manual installs need the [url=https://github.com/GrizzlyOne95/Battlezone98Redux_Shim/releases]complete OpenShim suite[/url] ([b]winmm.dll[/b], [b]bzloader.dll[/b], [b]plugins/openshim.dll[/b] and its config/assets), not winmm.dll alone. Remove other native DLL mods before troubleshooting.

[h2]Visual Remaster: Stock Assets Fixed and Rebuilt[/h2]
Most of the download is art. The stock models and textures are repaired and upgraded, and new terrain, skies, cockpits and UI are added.
[list]
[*] [b]Repaired stock models:[/b] about 240 stock vehicle, building and pilot meshes rebuilt with correct hard edges and fixed inside-out triangles, so hulls stop looking smeared or lit backwards. Skinned meshes no longer render flat grey in DX11, and the Soviet turret and walker cockpit views no longer flip or twitch.
[*] [b]New normal and detail maps:[/b] stock materials that shipped with flat normals get new normal maps derived from their textures, plus baked ambient occlusion, specular and glow work on relics, buildings, pickups and launch pads.
[*] [b]Revamped cockpits:[/b] 21 reworked interiors for NSDF, Black Dog, Soviet and Chinese craft. The glass cracks as your hull takes damage and collects rain, snow, dust and frost.
[*] [b]HD terrain on all nine worlds:[/b] new high-resolution ground, real crater relief on the Moon, wet ground and puddles in rain, Europa snow and glittering ice, glowing molten lava on Io and churning, bubbling sulphur on Venus.
[*] [b]New skies:[/b] a real star field and phase-lit Earth over the Moon, Jupiter at true size and phase (with eclipses) over Io, Europa and Ganymede, Saturn through Titan's haze, Uranus above Achilles' storms, dust and cirrus on Mars and a moving cloud deck on Venus.
[*] [b]New UI and loading screens:[/b] per-world loading screens, mission briefing images, new menu widgets and a DX11 HUD material.
[*] [b]New units and props:[/b] faction-styled nav beacons, pickups, storage and weapon crates, plus new mission buildings, capital ships, flora and Olympian relics.
[*] [b]Sound:[/b] new rain, thunder, lightning and waterfall effects and restored mission voice lines.
[/list]
[i]The remastered art loads inside Campaign Reimagined and its co-op maps. Terrain, liquid and weather effects need DX11 with the Enhanced renderer profile.[/i]

[h2]Game-Wide Engine Patch[/h2]
OpenShim isn't limited to this campaign. Its fixes work across the stock campaigns, Instant Action, multiplayer and compatible mods.
[list]
[*] [b]Big FPS gains:[/b] removed redundant geometry rebuilds, excess destruction-object submissions, broken craft culling and needless DX11 CPU/GPU syncs. 5-15% faster in typical CPU-heavy scenes, over 70% in destruction-heavy stress tests.
[*] [b]Destruction debris:[/b] destroyed vehicles and buildings break into physical chunks again, exactly like Battlezone 1.5, using the original hidden GEOs.
[*] [b]Multiplayer:[/b] netcode fixes for long matches, no more server list jumping or crash on game creation, no 30-second hang leaving a match, team flags over vehicles, host controls and persistent bans.
[*] [b]Native AutoSave:[/b] its own slot, in all single-player content including Instant Action.
[*] [b]Audio:[/b] a larger sound-channel pool, so fewer dropouts in big battles.
[*] [b]Crash diagnostics:[/b] native crash logs and minidumps that point at the real module and address.
[*] [b]Restored 1.5 behavior:[/b] working satellite fog of war (Redux shows the whole map), the classic HUD meter layout and the jump-snipe crouch (single-player).
[/list]

[h2]In-Game Options[/h2]
[list]
[*] [b]OpenShim Options page:[/b] raw mouse input, custom keybindings, attack alerts, target popups, HUD style, jet flames, unit voices, weapon convergence, smarter scavengers, anti-air turret pitch, global turbo and headlights. Most apply instantly, restart-only ones are marked, and hovering a row explains it.
[*] [b]Renderer profiles:[/b] stock-compatible Redux, Enhanced (with the DX11 features above) or retro presentation.
[*] [b]Rewritten key binding screen[/b] with live key capture, and a [b]Career stats[/b] main-menu button (enable it in OpenShim settings).
[/list]

[h2]Platform Support[/h2]
Windows and Linux (including Steam Deck, through Proton or Wine), on Steam and GOG. Both run the same 32-bit files and update together, so a difference between them is a bug worth reporting.

[h2]Uninstallation[/h2]
Delete [b]winmm.dll[/b] from the game folder to return to normal startup. The campaign will error without the patch, so unsubscribe for full removal.

[h2]Reporting Issues[/h2]
Please include reproduction steps rather than "it does not work." Detailed reports get fixed.

[h3]AI-Assisted Development[/h3]
I use Anthropic's Claude and OpenAI's GPT Sol models to speed up reverse engineering and long, tedious tasks. All work is designed, implemented, tested and reviewed by me.
